{#
	 ============================================================
		BOOTSWATCH SWITCHER  —  src/_includes/bootswatch-switcher.njk
	 ============================================================

	 Dev tool — lists all Bootswatch themes inside the offcanvas
	 menu.  Included conditionally via site.bootswatchSwitcher
	 in offcanvas-menu.njk.

	 To disable for production, set bootswatchSwitcher: false
	 in src/_data/site.json. The same switch drops
	 bootswatch-switcher.js from the bundle and the small restore
	 script from <head> (base.njk).

	 REQUIRES: bootswatch-switcher.js (in /assets/js/bundle.js) and
	 the window.ddBootswatchSheets map that base.njk writes into
	 <head> from src/_data/cdn.js (URL + SRI hash per theme).

	 THE LIST comes from cdn.js too — one button per theme there,
	 so a Bootswatch version bump is an edit in ONE file. The label
	 is the theme name with its first letter capitalised
	 (Nunjucks' `capitalize` filter: "darkly" → "Darkly").

	 COLLAPSE, NOT DROPDOWN — deliberate (ported from the fg project):
	 27 buttons is a lot of menu to scroll past, so the list is
	 folded away behind a toggle. It uses Bootstrap's `collapse`
	 rather than `dropdown` because a dropdown closes the moment
	 you click anything inside it, which is exactly wrong for a
	 style switcher — you want to click Cyborg, look, click Vapor,
	 look again, without re-opening the list every time. Collapse
	 ignores clicks on its contents and stays put.

	 No JS of our own for the collapse: data-bs-toggle="collapse"
	 is handled by the Bootstrap bundle that already powers the
	 offcanvas. Closed on every page load; picking a theme doesn't
	 navigate, so the list stays open while you try themes.

	 The header is a real <button> with aria-expanded (Bootstrap
	 updates it), so it is keyboard-reachable and announces whether
	 the list is open. It is styled like the other section labels
	 by .dd-offcanvas-section-toggle (style.css §4.4) but does NOT
	 carry the .dd-offcanvas-section class: high-contrast.css dims
	 that class to 70% opacity, which is meant for passive labels,
	 not for a control.

	 Options are toggle buttons (aria-pressed, set by the JS) in a
	 role="group" labelled by the header.
	 ============================================================
#}

<div class="dd-offcanvas-divider"></div>

<button type="button"
	class="dd-offcanvas-section-toggle collapsed"
	id="dd-bootswatch-toggle"
	data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#dd-bootswatch-collapse"
	aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="dd-bootswatch-collapse">
	<span><i class="bi bi-palette-fill me-1" aria-hidden="true"></i> Bootswatch</span>
	<i class="bi bi-chevron-down dd-offcanvas-section-caret" aria-hidden="true"></i>
</button>

<div class="collapse" id="dd-bootswatch-collapse" role="group" aria-labelledby="dd-bootswatch-toggle">
	<button type="button" class="nav-link dd-bootswatch-option" data-theme="default" aria-pressed="false">Bootstrap (Default)</button>
	{# `for key, value in object` loops over an object's entries; only the key (theme name) is needed here. #}
	{% for name, sheet in cdn.bootswatch.themes %}
	<button type="button" class="nav-link dd-bootswatch-option" data-theme="{{ name }}" aria-pressed="false">{{ name | capitalize }}</button>
	{% endfor %}
</div>
